---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout page={pages.disclaimer}>
  <h2>A development aid, with defined limits</h2>
  <p>
    These utilities assist with routine development tasks. They do not provide
    professional legal advice, a security audit, authentication decisions, or a
    guarantee that transformed data matches a particular business schema.
  </p>
  <h2>Decoding is not verification</h2>
  <p>
    The JWT decoder displays encoded claims without checking the signature,
    issuer, audience, or a server’s acceptance policy. A readable token or an
    unexpired timestamp does not establish trust. Base64 and percent encoding
    are reversible encodings, not encryption.
  </p>
  <h2>Check transformations before relying on them</h2>
  <p>
    JavaScript parses JSON numbers using binary floating-point precision.
    Duplicate object keys retain their final value with a warning. CSV cannot
    represent every JSON distinction. Regex syntax and time calculations follow
    the browser’s supported JavaScript APIs. Cron previews follow the explicitly
    documented parser and timezone behavior rather than every scheduler’s rules.
  </p>
  <h2>Local processing is not perfect security</h2>
  <p>
    Processing in the browser avoids uploading input as part of the core tool
    operation. It cannot protect against compromised devices, malicious
    extensions, browser history features, screenshots, or clipboard access by
    other software. Prefer sanitized, nonproduction examples and follow your
    organization’s data-handling rules.
  </p>
  <h2>No affiliation or approval claim</h2>
  <p>
    This website is an independent utility. References to protocols, products,
    and hosting services describe compatibility or provide documentation.
    Advertising preparation does not mean Google has approved the site, and
    performance targets are not measured scores unless a report explicitly
    states a measurement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> and each tool’s guide for further
    limitations.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
